maybe \u201cSeat Wind\u201d pung? No, W7 is not wind.  \n- The downside: I might lose chance for a concealed hand (Concealed Hand = 2 fan if win by discard).  \n- Current hand after two chows is already leaning toward All Simples + maybe Mixed Double Chow? Actually my melds are both in T suit, so not mixed.  \n\nIf I Pass and draw, I keep hand closed, possibly aim for:  \n- All Simples (2 fan)  \n- All Chows (if I get another chow)  \n- Possibly Half Flush? No, I have B suit tiles too.  \n- Wait for self-drawn win (1 fan) + maybe Edge/Closed Wait.  \n\nGiven remaining tiles: W7 has 3 left, so Peng now might block others from getting W7 pung/kong, but that\u2019s minor. More importantly, my hand is not close to high-value pattern (like Full Flush, etc.), so preserving flexibility is better.  \n\nAlso, Peng forces me to discard, possibly giving away useful tile. And I have two B5s \u2014 B5 is relatively safe (4 left unseen).  \n\nGiven the game stage (many discards), maybe I should Pass to keep hand concealed and try to draw into a Chow with W8 or B5/B6.  \n\n**Final choice:** Pass.  \n\n---\n\n**Answer:** Pass"}
