erent suits 123,456,789. But my melds are T6-T8 and T7-T9, which are not 123,456,789. So Mixed Straight requires specific chows: one each of 123, 456, 789 in different suits. My current melds: T6-T8 (456? T6 is 6, T7 7, T8 8 -> actually T6,T7,T8 is 6,7,8? Wait, T6,T7,T8 is chow 6-7-8. And T7,T8,T9 is 7-8-9. So I have 678 and 789 in same T suit. Not suitable for Mixed Straight.\n\nAlternative: \"Half Flush\" (6 points) + some other patterns. Half Flush requires only one suit and honors. My melds are both T suit, so if I can make my hand all T suit and honors, I could get Half Flush. Currently hand has W, B, F tiles. Would need to discard all non-T, non-honors. But I have F2 (honor), so could keep. But W and B need to be discarded. Possible, but long way.\n\nGiven I am already in ready state, I should discard a tile that keeps my waiting tiles as many as possible with high scoring potential.\n\nLet's analyze waits if I discard each:\n\nCurrent hand without considering melds: 8 tiles. Need 2 melds + pair. Suppose I keep pair W7, then need two melds from remaining: W5, W8, T7, B5, B6, F2. \n- Melds possible: Chow B5-B6 wait B4/B7; Chow W5-W7-W8? missing W6; Pung possibilities: need another W5, W8, F2, T7.\nSo likely my wait is for B4 or B7 to complete chow B4-B5-B6 or B5-B6-B7. And pair already W7. So then I would have: melds: (B4/B7 chow), (W7 pair), and two exposed chows. That's only 3 chows + pair, missing one meld. Actually, I need 4 melds total. I already have 2 melds exposed, so need 2 more from hand. So if I have chow from B5-B6 and pair W7, that's only 1 meld + pair, still need one more meld. So I must have another meld in hand. Could be: T7 can form chow with T5-T6 or T8-T9, but T5,T6,T8,T9 may be used or scarce. Or F2 pair to make pair and then W7 become part of meld? Let's try: If I make pair F2, then W7 must be part of meld: could be chow W5-W6-W7 or W6-W7-W8, waiting for W6. So possible waits: for B4/B7 to complete chow, and for W6 to complete chow, and pai