g points.\n- But I have no dragons.\n\nMaybe aim for \"All Chows\" (2) + \"Mixed Straight\" (8) if I can rearrange? Unlikely with current melds.\n\nPerhaps I should not be ready yet, and instead break the hand to aim for a better pattern. But the valid actions are only discards, no other actions like Chi, Peng, etc. So I must discard.\n\nGiven the state, I think the safest is to discard a tile that is safe (not likely to give other players pung/kong). Looking at game history: Next player has pung W5, so W5 is safe to discard? He already has pung, so discarding W5 won't give him another pung (needs 4th). But could give kong if he has concealed fourth? Possible but less likely. Similarly, previous player has chow B6-B8, so B5 or B6 might be safe? B5 could complete chow B4-B5-B6 or B5-B6-B7, but he already has B6-B7-B8, so B5 might be safe. \n\nBut I need to consider my own hand improvement.\n\nAfter evaluating, I think my best chance is to keep waits on B4/B7 and W6, and pair F2. So I need to discard tiles that are not part of these waits. From hand: W5, W7, W8, T7, B5, B6, F2. If I want waits on B4/B7 and W6, I need to keep B5, B6, W5, W7, W8, F2. That's 6 tiles, plus two W7? Actually I have two W7, so total 7 tiles: W5, W7, W7, W8, B5, B6, F2. Plus one more tile to discard? I have 8 tiles, so I need to discard one from these. Possibly discard T7, as it doesn't contribute. So discard T7.\n\nIf I discard T7, my hand: W5, W7, W7, W8, B5, B6, F2. Then I need one tile to complete. Possible completing tiles: \n- Draw W6: then I can form chow W5-W6-W7 and chow W6-W7-W8? But I have only two W7, so can't form two chows using same W7. Better: With W6, hand: W5, W6, W7, W7, W8, B5, B6, F2. Arrange: Pair W7? But then W5,W6,W7 chow, W7 used, leaving W8, B5, B6, F2. Not enough. Instead, pair F2. Then chows: W5-W6-W7, B5-B6-B7 (need B7), but I don't have B7. So not complete.\nMaybe wait for B4 or B7 to complete chow with B5-B6, and also need another meld from W tiles. If I get B4,